#: ../../../web_visualization.md:1
msgid "Overview"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../web_visualization.md:3
msgid ""
"Web visualization supports rendering and interacting with running Gazebo "
"simulations. You may find web visualization useful when interacting with "
"remote or headless Gazebo Sim simulations. No additionally dependencies, "
"other than a browser and internet connection, are required."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../web_visualization.md:9
msgid "How to use web visualization"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../web_visualization.md:11
msgid ""
"The following steps will guide you through the process of running Gazebo "
"with a websocket server and connecting to the websocket for visualization."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../web_visualization.md:15
msgid ""
"Start an Gazebo Sim instance as usual. We will use the `fuel.sdf` world and "
"run it headless."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../web_visualization.md:17
msgid "gz sim -v 4 -s -r fuel.sdf\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../web_visualization.md:21
msgid "Create an Gazebo Launch file with the websocket server plugin."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../web_visualization.md:22
msgid ""
"echo \"<?xml version='1.0'?>\n"
"<gz version='1.0'>\n"
"  <plugin name='gz::launch::WebsocketServer'\n"
"          filename='gz-launch-websocket-server'>\n"
"    <port>9002</port>\n"
"  </plugin>\n"
"</gz>\" > websocket.gzlaunch\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../web_visualization.md:32
msgid "Run the websocket server using"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../web_visualization.md:33
msgid "gz launch -v 4 websocket.gzlaunch\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../web_visualization.md:37
msgid ""
"Visualize the simulation by going to [https://app.gazebosim.org/"
"visualization](https://app.gazebosim.org/visualization) and pressing the "
"Connect button."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../web_visualization.md:40
msgid ""
"It may take a few seconds for the scene to load. Your browser needs to fetch "
"all of the models in the world."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../web_visualization.md:43
msgid "Websocket server customization"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../web_visualization.md:45
msgid "The following parameters are available in the websocket server plugin."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../web_visualization.md:47
msgid ""
"`<admin_authorization_key>` : If this is set, then a connection must provide "
"the matching key using an \"auth\" call on the websocket. If the "
"`<authorization_key>` is set, then the connection can provide that key."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../web_visualization.md:48
msgid ""
"`<authorization_key>` : If this is set, then a connection must provide the "
"matching key using an \"auth\" call on the websocket. If the "
"`<admin_authorization_key>` is set, then the connection can provide that key."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../web_visualization.md:50
msgid ""
"`<max_connections>` : An integer that is the maximum number of simultaneous "
"connections."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../web_visualization.md:51
msgid "`<port>` : An integer that is websocket port."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../web_visualization.md:52
msgid ""
"`<publication_hz>` : An integer that is the maximum publication hertz rate."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../web_visualization.md:54
msgid "Code and Support"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../web_visualization.md:56
msgid ""
"The code for the web application, [app.gazebosim.org](https://app.gazebosim."
"org), lives at [https://github.com/gazebo-web/gazebosim-app](https://github."
"com/gazebo-web/gazebosim-app)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../web_visualization.md:60
msgid ""
"The javascript library used to render the 3D scene lives at [https://github."
"com/gazebo-web/gzweb](https://github.com/gazebo-web/gzweb)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../web_visualization.md:63
msgid ""
"Is you notice an issue with web visualization, then please file a ticket at "
"[https://github.com/gazebo-web/gzweb/issues](https://github.com/gazebo-web/"
"gzweb/issues)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../web_visualization.md:67
msgid "Troubleshooting"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../web_visualization.md:69
msgid ""
"If you are running Gazebo Sim in a docker container, make sure to use the [--"
"network host](https://docs.docker.com/network/network-tutorial-host/) Docker "
"commandline option. Without `--network host` the web application won't be "
"able to connect to the websocket server."
msgstr ""
